{
  "language_code": "en",
  "text": "Is it possible for a genuinely private person to build a personal brand? Two years ago, I would've told you, no. You see, there was a point where I was posting outfit videos every single week because that allowed me to stay hidden. I could be online every single day without ever saying one thing I truly thought. And I would spend entire days filming, but my account never really turned into anything real, anything of substance, anything of value, until I figured out what a personal brand is actually made of. It's your opinions, your lessons, and your story. Your private life, though, can still stay private. So I wrote down everything I refused to share, and then I spoke freely about everything else that I was okay with sharing. And in just six months, my videos started bringing in the community of a woman, the audience that I truly, deeply wanted to build. And all of this became a real business. Building a personal brand is actually simpler than you think. You're just sharing the wrong things. If you're tired and overwhelmed and just confused with what to post and how to show up, comment scene down below and we'll work on this together.",
